<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akbar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1556–1605</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Akbar was the third Mughal emperor, reigning from 1556 to 1605. He expanded the empire across most of northern and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and built an efficient administration based on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansabdari-system">mansabdari</a> system and a reformed land revenue. His policy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/religious-tolerance">religious tolerance</a> and alliances with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> rulers made him one of the most important figures in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/akbar.jpg" alt="Akbar" width="311" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Govardhan / Mir Ali Heravi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Govardhan._Akbar_With_Lion_and_Calf_ca._1630,_Metmuseum_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
